Design:

```julia
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# T01-D · F-15: casos dirigidos de NONCE por clave de garantía
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Punto del bloque negativo y estado promovido (reutiliza `bloque_neg`).
function _contexto_nonce(P::Params, pref::Vector{Bloque}, Ep::Estado, Bk::Bloque)
    es_pow = Bk.familia == PoW
    fase = es_pow ? FasePoW : FasePoST
    pt = punto_bloque_neg(Ep, Bk)
    Ef = estado_promovido(Ep, P, fase, pt)
    prod_ok = activo_de(Ef, 1) >= UInt64(P.q)
    return es_pow, fase, pt, Ef, prod_ok
end

# Añade un caso de bloque negativo `[coinbase, txs...]` con el error esperado.
function _agrega_nonce!(out, P, pref, Ep, Bk, nombre, familia, esperado, txs;
                        productor = 1, peso = 1)
    B = bloque_neg(P, pref, Ep, Bk, txs; productor = productor, peso = peso)
    push!(out, CasoNegativo(nombre, esperado, Bk.familia == PoW ? "PoW" : "PoST",
                            familia, vcat(pref, [B])))
end
```

Hmm, `bloque_neg` signature: `bloque_neg(P, pref, Ep, Bk, txs; productor=1, peso=1)`. Good.

Now the main per-block generator:

```julia
function casos_nonce_bloque(P::Params, pref::Vector{Bloque}, Ep::Estado, Bk::Bloque)
    out = CasoNegativo[]
    es_pow, fase, pt, Ef, prod_ok = _contexto_nonce(P, pref, Ep, Bk)
    (es_pow || prod_ok) || return out
    cb() = es_pow ? tx_coinbase([salida_neg(970000 + 37*Ep.altura + 7*length(pref), 10, 1)]) :
                    tx_coinbase_post(3)
    # `salida_neg` ids must not collide; use a counter via Ref.
    ...
```

Wait, `cb()` must produce a unique output id per case to avoid ErrDobleGasto in the block. In `casos_bloque`, `oid = Ref(900000 + 37*last(pref).id)` and `nuevo()` increments. I'll do the same.

Let me structure with a local `oid = Ref(970000 + 37*last(pref).id + (es_pow ? 0 : 500000))` and `nuevo() = (oid[] += 1; oid[])`.

```julia
function casos_nonce_bloque(P::Params, pref::Vector{Bloque}, Ep::Estado, Bk::Bloque)
    out = CasoNegativo[]
    es_pow = Bk.familia == PoW
    fase = es_pow ? FasePoW : FasePoST
    pt = punto_bloque_neg(Ep, Bk)
    Ef = estado_promovido(Ep, P, fase, pt)
    prod_ok = activo_de(Ef, 1) >= UInt64(P.q)
    (es_pow || prod_ok) || return out
    oid = Ref(970000 + 37 * last(pref).id + (es_pow ? 0 : 500000))
    nuevo() = (oid[] += 1; oid[])
    cb() = es_pow ? tx_coinbase([salida_neg(nuevo(), 10, 1)]) : tx_coinbase_post(3)
    prod = 1
    peso = 1

    # Ops ya aplicadas en `pref` (repetición): el nonce es viejo.
    for (b, tx) in ((b, tx) for b in pref for tx in b.txs)
        (tx.tipo == TxRetiro || tx.tipo == TxLiberacion) || continue
        eti = tx.tipo == TxRetiro ? "retiro" : "liberacion"
        familia = tx.tipo == TxRetiro ? "NonceRepRetiro" : "NonceRepLiberacion"
        # El prefijo solo trae bloques válidos; la repetición debe dar ErrNonce.
        if !es_pow && !prod_ok
            continue
        end
        _agrega_nonce!(out, P, pref, Ep, Bk,
                       "neg-nonce-rep-" * eti, familia, ErrNonce,
                       [cb(), _copia_tx(tx)]; productor = prod, peso = peso)
    end
    ...
```

Hmm, but `_agrega_nonce!` calls `bloque_neg` which creates the block; `cb()` is evaluated when building txs, before the call. Fine.

But wait: for a redirect, `Tx` is immutable; replaying the same `tx` object is fine (no mutation). But `txs` vector will contain the same object; `aplicar_txs!` doesn't mutate txs. So no need to copy. But to be safe, `deepcopy(tx)`? `Tx` contains vectors; `aplicar` doesn't mutate them. I'll just reuse `tx`.

However, there's a subtle issue: if `pref` contains multiple retiros (2), we generate a repetition case for each retiro in each block. That's fine.

But more importantly: the block `B` built by `bloque_neg` has `txs = [cb(), tx]`. The coinbase output id from `cb()` might collide with an existing UTXO? `bloque_neg` uses `gen_pow(id = tip+1, ...)`. The coinbase output id is `nuevo()` which is 970000+... These shouldn't collide with existing. Good.

